  ## Three Possible Outcomes, $N_{t+1 = N_t + N_tr$}
  ::: columns
    ::: {.column width='50%'}
      \small
      \centering
      If $-1 \leq r < 0$ \\ population goes extinct \\
      ![](figs/rl0)
    :::
    ::: {.column width='50%'}
      \small
      \centering
      If $r = 0$ \\ population is stable \\
      ![](figs/r0)
    :::
    ::: {.column width='50%'}
      \small
      \centering
      If $r > 0$ \\ population grows to $\infty$ \\
      ![](figs/rg0)
    :::
  :::








